# EXPECT_RUNTIME_ERROR
#~
A program that dies inside the VM must leave obr with a non-zero exit status.

Execute (core/vm/vm.cpp) catches an exception that escapes the interpreter,
prints ">>> virtual machine: internal error: ... <<<" and returns -1. The
POSIX entry point (core/vm/posix_main.cpp) discarded that result and returned
0, so on Linux and macOS such a program reported success to whatever ran it --
a shell, a Makefile, a CI step -- and only a reader of stderr knew. Windows
returned the -1.

The way in is Runtime->SetProperty("runtime.test.throw", ...), a key the VM
reserves for exactly this: SetSysProp (core/vm/common.cpp) throws a
std::runtime_error carrying the value, so the exception reaches Execute's
catch, or under compiled code the bridge's, on every platform and in every VM
mode.

No correct trap throws, so this catch has no other honest trigger. The file
used to ride on defects: "1e999"->ToFloat() until String->ToFloat stopped
throwing std::out_of_range, then a float precision property that was not a
number until Runtime->SetProperty refused one (vm_parse_ranges.obs). Each fix
took the trigger away; the reserved key does not depend on any of them. The
case first seen, on macOS, was Runtime->SetProperty("locale", "xx_YY.bogus")
dying with "locale constructed with null"; #774 makes that call survive.

The regression runner passes this file only on a non-zero exit WITH output,
which is exactly the fix: the old obr printed the line and exited 0.

With every method compiled (OBJECK_JIT_THRESHOLD=1, --jit=1) the exception is
thrown inside the interpreter callback that the compiled Main made. Until #778
it could not unwind through the JIT'd frame: libc++ terminated the process
before Execute's catch, and the runner's second pass could not count an abort
as its expected error. The bridge now catches the exception and reports it as
Execute does -- the line, the stack, exit status 1 -- so both passes run this
file in their own mode, and run_vm_flag_tests.py (section 7) checks the status
under --jit=1 as well.
~#

class VmErrorExit {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		"before"->PrintLine();
		Runtime->SetProperty("runtime.test.throw", "deliberate test exception");
		"after"->PrintLine();
	}
}
